1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Ugh, is this even the right way?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,000
It definitely is.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Are you sure?

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Stop!

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Pick up the pace!

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Tell that to the others!

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Hey now, don't push!

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
I remembered this all.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
This is where we fought the Red Dragon.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,000
I see.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
So you came all the way out here on your last expedition?

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Yeah.

13
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
This was thought to be the deepest part of the dungeon for a while.

14
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
But recently, someone found a door around here that seems to lead farther in.

15
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
There were patterns engraved on it, so it was thought to open with magic.

16
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
The Island Lord asked us to come copy the patterns for him, but then...

17
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
You ran into the Red Dragon and eventually had to retreat.

18
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Alright, let's test our luck.

19
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
I think we were around there last time.

20
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Hey!

21
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Found our stuff!

22
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Huh?

23
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,000
It's been ransacked.

24
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Oh no!

25
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Heck yeah!

26
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,000
I found my sleeping bag!

27
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Thank God!

28
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,000
My underwear survived!

29
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
You checked for that stuff first instead of money, huh?

30
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,000
It seems like all the food we had was taken.

31
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
But everything else is here.

32
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Safe to assume monsters did this.

33
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,000
This is great!

34
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Now I'll be all warm when I fall off!

35
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,000
That's bad.

36
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Let's find a place where we can rest for a bit.

37
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Gives me time to sort my things.

38
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
I wonder if the snow makes the cleaners slow down at all.

39
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Something nibbled on my soul!

40
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Hey you!

41
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Remove whatever you just put in your pocket.

42
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Hey Marcel, catch!

43
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Huh?

44
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
You're not really well trained for a beast man.

45
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
I'm starting to realize where they'd probably put that collar on you.

46
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
You're one of those half-foots, I'm assuming.

47
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
I'd only just heard of them since there aren't any in the East.

48
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
I'd never seen one till coming here.

49
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
The name of your race is pretty strange.

50
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:11,000
I heard it came from your kind getting one of their legs chopped off due to committing too much thievery.

51
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Come on you two, there's no need for that.

52
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Marcel!

53
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Come here!

54
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Oh, you found fish!

55
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Is there a way for us to cut out this uncovered part right here?

56
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
I could maybe do it with a magic circle.

57
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,000
That's right!

58
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Do you want to give it a try?

59
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
I can teach you how to draw one if you do.

60
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
How's your mana sickness been lately?

61
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
I haven't been staggering as much.

62
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
The hallucinations have gotten a lot worse though.

63
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
I caught this fish a lot on the fourth floor.

64
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Is the water flowing in from the upper floors freezing once it gets down here?

65
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Seems a lot of stuff got washed up in this place.

66
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
And that completes the circle.

67
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,000
How are you feeling?

68
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
A bit tired honestly.

69
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Well, let me activate it then.

70
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
All you've got to do is...

71
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Imagine water filling these symbols and...

72
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,000
What's this?

73
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
The floor's moving!

74
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
A monster!

75
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,000
There?

76
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,000
That thing is an ice golem.

77
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Hmm...

78
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
I see.

79
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Above you!

80
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Look out!

81
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,000
My house!

82
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
There's a fish!

83
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
There's a fish!

84
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
There's too much crap in it!

85
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Hey, uh...

86
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
How do I kill this big snowman?

87
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
It's a golem, so you're gonna have to destroy its core!

88
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Core?

89
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Where would that even...

90
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Where would that even...

91
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Well?

92
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Where is it?

93
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Give me a sec!

94
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Is that it?

95
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,000
No, that's a fish.

96
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Yeah, there's too much crap in it!

97
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Hey!

98
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Try to distract the enemy to buy me time!

99
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
I still need to find the car!

100
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Huh?!

101
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,000
That bastard.

102
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,000
How do I know he's not lying?

103
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
This better not be a trick or something.

104
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,000
The snow!

105
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
The snow!

106
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Why'd it stop moving?

107
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Look!

108
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Can you hurry?

109
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
How long do I have to keep this up?

110
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,000
You're good!

111
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
That was long enough!

112
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Yes!

113
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Nailed it!

114
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Idiot!

115
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Do you think this is a game?

116
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
You're the idiots!

117
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Check out!

118
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
We're the hero idiots!

119
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,000
By the way!

120
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
While I am able to use ranged weapons,

121
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
I can't exactly do that much damage with any of them!

122
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
So you better not go counting on me in a fight!

123
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,000
The rest is up to you!

124
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Fine.

125
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
As long as I know how to kill it.

126
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:53,000
It looks like I'm the only one in the group who's agile enough to take on an enemy that big!

127
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Can't believe how slow you guys are!

128
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,000
I...

129
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,000
I...

130
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,000
I...

131
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
I...

132
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,000
I...

133
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
I...

134
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
I...

135
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
I...

136
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:10,000
I...

137
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
I....

138
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,000
I...

139
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,000
I...

140
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
I...

141
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
I...

142
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,000
I...

143
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Are all of you doing ok?

144
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,000
It'll start to warm up soon!

145
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:24,400
Okay, it'll start to warm up soon. That magic circle will get hot, so please be careful not to burn yourselves.

146
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:30,620
Take off all your wet clothes so we can dry them. That means you too. Here, I'll hold this up to cover you.

147
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:32,820
Do you need help with yours, Laios?

148
00:06:34,660 --> 00:06:36,340
Could one of you guys help him out?

149
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:40,140
You really don't have to do that, you know.

150
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:42,380
No, it's not that big of a deal.

151
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:54,780
Not like anyone's gonna get excited over a beast getting naked.

152
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:57,100
What the hell are you doing?

153
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:59,540
Well, it would be bad if you felt colder.

154
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:02,940
At least tell me the number of nipples and where the tail connection is...

155
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:12,320
It's finally gotten warmer in here. I'll start fixing up a hot meal for everyone.

156
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:15,300
But first, I need to thaw this.

157
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:18,200
Might as well melt it with the magic circle.

158
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:22,800
Must have been too close.

159
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:25,980
Wow, but this is actually nice. It's like a sauna.

160
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:30,340
We haven't been able to take a bath for a while, so let's sweat it out a little bit.

161
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:37,060
Wait, that comes off?

162
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:38,500
Why is it only me?

163
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:42,020
Gut the fish and then make a broth from the head and bones.

164
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:45,060
I feel like we're gonna smell like fish after this.

165
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:48,020
Finally, slice a couple mushrooms and nightmares.

166
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:52,220
Lightly boil the shapeshifter meat and remove any scum that forms.

167
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:57,380
Beat some harpy eggs and then add that mixture to the broth along with all the other ingredients.

168
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:02,220
Pour all that into cups.

169
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:06,980
Place the cups into the pan with ice golem fragments and put over a fire.

170
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:10,000
Look, I made this from her fur.

171
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:11,200
Bored much?

172
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:14,400
Lastly, place some mandrake leaves over the top and...

173
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:15,900
It's red...

174
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:17,040
Hey!

175
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:19,380
Don't just start eating on your own.

176
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:22,260
You've gotta wait until everyone gathers at the table.

177
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:23,460
Why should I wait?

178
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,700
I defeated that thing all by myself!

179
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:28,420
I think I deserve to eat before the rest of you!

180
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:31,440
A meal's something you only start when everyone's together.

181
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:32,580
Chill, Chuck.

182
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:33,760
Lios is outside.

183
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:35,260
Mind calling him back in?

184
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:36,060
Sure thing.

185
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:38,980
Oh, this feels great.

186
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:40,320
Is this guy for real?

187
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:47,800
Now that everyone's gathered, I think it's that time.

188
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,100
So let's eat!

189
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:50,760
Let's read it in!

190
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,240
It's pudding.

191
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:54,960
Oops!

192
00:08:55,220 --> 00:08:56,060
Sorry, Marcel.

193
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:56,840
Delicious!

194
00:08:57,900 --> 00:08:59,460
What a waste of time.

195
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:00,900
Hey, Yuzutsumi.

196
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,040
What is it?

197
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:03,320
This is for you.

198
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:06,160
I sewed up one of the bags that got ripped.

199
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:07,240
You should use it.

200
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:13,880
And, uh, I'm sorry I called you a beast before.

201
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:16,320
I have a notoriously foul mouth.

202
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:20,740
You know, traveling with a group of strangers can be uncomfortable.

203
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:24,240
But once you get used to it, you'll see the advantages.

204
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:27,640
You can rely on them to handle things for you.

205
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:29,680
Um...

206
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:31,680
Uh...

207
00:09:31,680 --> 00:09:37,880
Thank you for the good meal!

208
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:40,080
Thanks.

209
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:44,560
Come on, are you done yet?

210
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:45,380
Almost.

211
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:46,580
Just a second.

212
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:50,000
This goes here, and...

213
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:50,340
Done!

214
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,260
Ta-da!

215
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:57,700
Their Namaari's close, but they're perfect, right?

216
00:09:57,860 --> 00:09:59,080
It's hard to move.

217
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:01,560
It did take a while to take them in, though.

218
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,200
Yeah, now I'm cold again.

219
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,400
Look, I'm sorry.

220
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:05,980
Let's start heading out now.

221
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:06,640
Hold on.

222
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:09,260
Great.

223
00:10:09,260 --> 00:10:11,820
I boiled the mandrakes in some sweet sauce.

224
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:14,700
Figured it'd be a good thing to snack on while we walked.

225
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:19,580
Hey.

226
00:10:21,260 --> 00:10:21,780
Here.

227
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,260
But this belongs to you.

228
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,040
Don't want it.

229
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,120
Why?

230
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:29,600
It's really good.

231
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,740
I said I don't want the thing!

232
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:32,440
Oh, come on.

233
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:33,680
Just try a little bite.

234
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:34,340
Here.

235
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:35,580
Cut it now!

236
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:39,380
Oh, horrible.

237
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:42,600
We've been walking for two seconds, and there's already blood drawn.

238
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,100
Hey, just leave her be.

239
00:10:44,340 --> 00:10:45,480
She'll eat when she gets hungry.

240
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:48,220
So why don't you want to eat it?

241
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:49,480
It's a monster.

242
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:51,040
Everyone says that.

243
00:10:51,140 --> 00:10:52,840
But how is it different than eating an animal?

244
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:56,720
If you eat monsters, you'll get a weird disease and then transform into one.

245
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:57,720
So no thank you!

246
00:10:58,220 --> 00:11:01,580
Things would be so much easier if that was something that actually happened.

247
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:07,340
Monsters are believed to be unclean, and it's obviously not entirely logical, but that's

248
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:10,120
the reason most people, including me, find it gross.

249
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:13,240
You just get this feeling that you'll absorb something bad.

250
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:18,260
New diseases spring up from creatures coming in contact with humans all the time, so it's

251
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:21,060
not fair to question why someone doesn't feel like eating monsters.

252
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:22,320
Mmm!

253
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:25,680
This is really tasty!

254
00:11:26,460 --> 00:11:29,200
By the way, when you had to eat food you didn't like...

255
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:31,280
How did you go about handling that exactly?

256
00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:33,740
What did I do?

257
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:36,880
Ugh.

258
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,900
Here, Tade, you can have this.

259
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:43,900
Thanks, Isu!

260
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:45,440
Me nice to be!

261
00:11:45,760 --> 00:11:47,120
That never happened.

262
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:48,560
There's no way!

263
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:49,360
Come on, you two!

264
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,000
Let's go!

265
00:11:50,000 --> 00:12:03,840
This storm probably won't die down any time soon.

266
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:06,140
Then let's set up camp around this area.

267
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:07,640
I'm getting hungry.

268
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:09,800
But Senshi fell asleep.

269
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,280
We can prep a meal in the meantime.

270
00:12:13,140 --> 00:12:14,860
What ingredients do we have left?

271
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:19,760
There's nightmares and a mandrake, eggs and some mushrooms, whatever this is.

272
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:20,540
Got any fish?

273
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:21,160
Nope.

274
00:12:21,340 --> 00:12:22,280
We're all out of that.

275
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:23,240
Rice, then?

276
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:26,060
We're actually pretty low on rice as well.

277
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:28,820
Don't you have anything better than this gross stuff?

278
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:29,920
This is everything.

279
00:12:30,260 --> 00:12:30,740
Liar!

280
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,160
You're hiding it from me.

281
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:34,780
You can't be a picky eater when you're inside a dungeon.

282
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:36,860
So you should get used to trying things.

283
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:37,320
No!

284
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:39,400
I only eat the things I want to eat!

285
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:40,800
Please just listen.

286
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:43,280
Eating monsters isn't going to turn you into one.

287
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:46,840
Do people who eat pigs and sheep turn into either of those animals?

288
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:50,940
If someone who was blind ate an eyeball, would they regain their sight?

289
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:54,240
Sheep only eat plants, but they stay sheep, don't they?

290
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:57,880
Food and nutrition are more complex than you might think they are.

291
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:00,620
That's why people are still conducting research.

292
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,160
I'm sick of all your lies!

293
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:04,000
How in the hell do you explain that, then?

294
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,040
Explain what?

295
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:11,520
A tree actually grew a sheep.

296
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:13,360
That's a baromets.

297
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:16,360
But to think it would actually show up at a time like this...

298
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:19,380
So, first of all, that kind of plant is always like...

299
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:19,800
Shut it!

300
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,680
I'm sick of all your yammering!

301
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:22,920
Whatever, man.

302
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,160
I'm gonna go catch that sheep.

303
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:26,160
What's a baromets?

304
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:26,920
A monster?

305
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:29,940
That's what it's classified as, but it's harmless.

306
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:33,660
However, what's not harmless is they attract carnivores.

307
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:36,200
Careful, Izutsumi!

308
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:38,160
I don't need your warnings.

309
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:42,320
And we shouldn't linger.

310
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:43,900
Let's harvest it and then...

311
00:13:43,900 --> 00:13:44,220
Quiet.

312
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:45,400
Huh?

313
00:13:49,880 --> 00:13:50,360
Crap!

314
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:51,480
A direwolf pack!

315
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:58,680
I need a staff!

316
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:04,900
Hey, hold it!

317
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,260
Where are you going?

318
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:08,020
I'm not a fan of dogs.

319
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:09,900
They're annoying and they smell bad.

320
00:14:10,820 --> 00:14:13,340
That's your reasoning for coming in here all on your own?

321
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:15,580
I'm relying on them.

322
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:19,820
Depending on your party members to pick up your slack is your idea of teamwork, isn't it?

323
00:14:19,820 --> 00:14:22,060
Uh, no, that's...

324
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:23,360
That's not what that means at all!

325
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,080
What do you mean?

326
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,980
You didn't fight when we were dealing with that ice golem earlier.

327
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:31,360
It's true I relied on you guys back then, but it wasn't because I didn't want to help out.

328
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:34,780
Uh, hey, why don't we go back?

329
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:35,700
No thanks.

330
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:38,460
I smell fire on the wind.

331
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:41,280
If we follow it, we'll get back to where we came from.

332
00:14:42,660 --> 00:14:43,860
Hey, wait up!

333
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:50,180
The path to the right smells like the campfire, but it looks rough, so left it is.

334
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:51,620
Do you know where you're going?

335
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:52,880
Is this the right direction?

336
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,380
I take whatever path I like the best.

337
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:57,080
You should learn to do that, too.

338
00:14:57,620 --> 00:14:59,540
Why bother doing things you don't want to do?

339
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:03,960
You eat monsters, even though you don't really want to eat them.

340
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:06,020
It doesn't make any sense.

341
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,740
Well, I mean...

342
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:11,620
I think the wolves are coming after us.

343
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:12,980
Should we try to fight them?

344
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:17,480
I'm typically able to use explosive magic, but I don't have my staff right now.

345
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:21,800
It's too cramped in here anyway, so I could stun them with a really bright light, maybe.

346
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,400
Let's just lose them!

347
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:28,020
Whoaaaa!

348
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:45,240
Howie!

349
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:54,060
Hey! Get back here, Asebi!

350
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:58,540
Fess up. You made Tade shovel snow for you, didn't you?

351
00:15:59,260 --> 00:15:59,740
Nope.

352
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:03,540
Don't lie to me! She fell off the training hall roof because of that!

353
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:05,900
Unlike you, Tade is incredibly clumsy.

354
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:08,400
So don't shove jobs you don't like onto her.

355
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:11,020
Show some gratitude for us taking you in.

356
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:13,500
Nah.

357
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:15,940
Hey, Tade.

358
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:19,180
Why'd you do something I never asked you for?

359
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,420
You're such an idiot.

360
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:23,240
But Tade just...

361
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:27,660
What was it that Tade said to me back then?

362
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:29,960
It doesn't matter.

363
00:16:35,400 --> 00:16:36,600
I messed up.

364
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:40,540
The blast changed the wind's direction, so I missed this one.

365
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:47,620
Cl-close your eyes.

366
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:49,920
Close your eyes.

367
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:50,980
Do it!

368
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:52,320
Now!

369
00:16:52,320 --> 00:17:02,320
I can't...

370
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,500
I... I can't...

371
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:11,180
I... I...

372
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:13,080
Is it Tade?

373
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:14,640
Are you alive?

374
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:15,920
Oh...

375
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:20,620
Your arm is broken. Can you move? Let's go and find the others.

376
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:32,280
Listen. You wanted to know why I eat monsters, didn't you?

377
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:37,380
I've been thinking about it, and I have multiple goals that I want to accomplish.

378
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:41,820
Like rescuing my best friend and learning everything I can about magic.

379
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:48,440
So, while working to achieve all my goals, I sometimes run into things that I don't like.

380
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:53,620
Something bothersome, or tiring, or having to eat something I really don't want to.

381
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:57,820
None of those things are bad on their own, but...

382
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:03,180
If I continued avoiding them, I'd keep getting further and further away from my path, right?

383
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:06,100
Exactly like we're doing in this cave.

384
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:10,780
I'm curious. Why did you decide to come along with us?

385
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:17,160
Are you stupid? Because you told me I needed to find that mad whatever guy to even have a chance to break this curse!

386
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:18,240
Now follow me!

387
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:23,120
Exactly. And that means we probably won't be able to take the easy path there.

388
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:32,680
Izutsumi! Marcil! You're both okay!

389
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:34,860
You guys are okay too, right?

390
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:37,340
Not really, but at least we're all in one piece.

391
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:40,980
We have Laios' intimidation skills to thank for that.

392
00:18:41,140 --> 00:18:43,980
It helps that most of the wolves went after you, Marcil.

393
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:45,400
You hurt?

394
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:47,540
I think her arm is broken.

395
00:18:48,140 --> 00:18:51,660
Would you be able to help me out while I'm casting a healing spell on it, Laios?

396
00:18:51,660 --> 00:18:59,260
You did great, Izutsumi!

397
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:02,200
The healing spell hurt more than breaking it.

398
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:07,500
I was planning on harvesting the baromets, but all the ripe ones were taken by the dire wolves.

399
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,780
This was the only one left for grabs, but it's not ready yet.

400
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:13,780
Let's see if we can cook it.

401
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:23,900
There's a little sheep inside the vegetable.

402
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:24,960
I can't!

403
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:27,860
For a completely different ethical reason, I refuse!

404
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:32,660
First, cut up the baromets' ribs into whatever portions you want.

405
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:34,900
Season them and put them on the fire.

406
00:19:35,620 --> 00:19:37,880
After both sides of each have been nicely browned,

407
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:41,560
add wine over top, cover the pan, and then braise them.

408
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:47,100
Next, boil the remainder of the fruit, peel off the skin, and cut it into chunks.

409
00:19:47,620 --> 00:19:49,860
Add some garlic and simmer all of it together.

410
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:54,420
With the sauce finished, you take that, pour it over the meat, and...

411
00:19:54,420 --> 00:19:55,200
It's ready!

412
00:19:58,220 --> 00:19:59,780
This helping's yours, Catgirl.

413
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:00,900
Go on, take it.

414
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:03,740
What's all the weird-looking stuff?

415
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:06,700
It's the skin of the baromets, fruit, and a handful of sprouts.

416
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:11,440
You could have just fried the meat and been done with it.

417
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:20,060
The baromets.

418
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:21,960
It may resemble an everyday sheep,

419
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:23,560
but it tastes more like crab!

420
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:24,860
That doesn't make it better!

421
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:27,100
This is so good.

422
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:29,700
I didn't know something this delicious could exist.

423
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,300
Wait, that reminds me.

424
00:20:33,060 --> 00:20:36,280
Tade, why'd you do something that I never asked you for?

425
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:38,440
You're such an idiot.

426
00:20:39,580 --> 00:20:40,280
Tade just wants...

427
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:43,860
to be as accommodating as she can to everyone.

428
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:47,000
Because this place is amazing!

429
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:48,360
Three meals a day,

430
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:49,700
a bath to keep clean,

431
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:50,980
and a cozy photon!

432
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:53,780
I definitely cannot get myself kicked out of here!

433
00:20:54,020 --> 00:20:56,660
I will do even the smallest chore to show I'm useful!

434
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:59,460
Hey, Asabi.

435
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:03,460
Don't get discouraged just because of some minor inconveniences.

436
00:21:03,460 --> 00:21:08,100
Oh, and if I do good,

437
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:10,300
Lady Miser will give me treats sometimes!

438
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:12,500
So that's what you're really after, huh?

439
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:14,960
Guess this is what she meant.

440
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:18,340
Sometimes you get tasty things out of doing what you don't wanna.

441
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:23,180
Good job!

442
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:24,880
I'm proud of you, Izutsumi!

443
00:21:24,940 --> 00:21:26,180
You did so well today!

444
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:27,580
Way to go, bud!

445
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:28,960
Turn it out, you bastards!

446
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:30,800
What do you think you're doing?!

447
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:32,160
Don't touch me!

448
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:35,600
I only ate it because I had no other choice!

449
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:38,520
You'll never see me eat gross veggies or monsters again!

450
00:21:39,060 --> 00:21:41,680
You won't know if they're gross or not till you try them, though.

451
00:21:42,260 --> 00:21:43,120
By the way, Marcel,

452
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:45,220
you've barely touched your food.

453
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:47,540
After all the lecturing you gave me earlier,

454
00:21:47,660 --> 00:21:49,400
don't you even try to get out of eating.

455
00:21:50,840 --> 00:21:55,040
Marcel deeply regretted being the one to close off her own escape route.

456
00:21:55,820 --> 00:21:57,340
Ah, dungeon food.

457
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,300
Delicious in dungeon.

